Below is a quick “map” of the columns that matter for the requested data‑set, followed by a set of step‑by‑step BigQuery sample queries (from exploratory to the final combined view).

-------------------------------------------------
Key columns & how they will be used
-------------------------------------------------
`mbb_historical_tournament_games`
 • season            : season filter (>= 2014) & join key to metrics  
 • win_seed          : seed when outcome = win  
 • win_school_ncaa   : winner’s school name – join key to metrics  
 • lose_seed         : seed when outcome = loss  
 • lose_school_ncaa  : loser’s school name – join key to metrics  

`2018_tournament_results`
 • season            : always 2018, keeps the same join logic  
 • label             : ‘win’ / ‘loss’ already supplied  
 • seed              : team seed (matches “win_seed/lose_seed”)  
 • school_ncaa       : team name – join key to metrics  
 • opponent_seed     : seed of opponent  
 • opponent_school_ncaa : opponent name – join key to metrics  

`feature_engineering`
 • season            : join key  
 • team              : school name (matches *_school_ncaa)  
 • poss_40min        : new pace metric  
 • pace_rating       : pace rating  
 • pace_rank         : pace rank  
 • pts_100poss       : new efficiency metric  
 • efficiency_rating : efficiency rating  
 • efficiency_rank   : efficiency rank  

-------------------------------------------------
Typical conditions we will apply
-------------------------------------------------
1. `WHERE season >= 2014`                       -- only modern era  
2. `WHERE school_ncaa IS NOT NULL`              -- avoid blanks  
3. String‑match join `ON LOWER(team)=LOWER(school_ncaa)`  
4. Left joins for metrics (some small schools may not have data)  

-------------------------------------------------
BigQuery examples (10 queries)
-------------------------------------------------
Each query is capped with `LIMIT 20` just for inspection purposes.

```sql
-- 1. Seasons available in the historical tournament file, 2014+
SELECT DISTINCT season
FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
WHERE season >= 2014
ORDER BY season;
```

```sql
-- 2. Sample 2014+ winners (one row per game winner)
SELECT season,
       win_seed   AS seed,
       win_school_ncaa AS school_ncaa,
       lose_school_ncaa AS opponent_school_ncaa
FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
WHERE season >= 2014
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Sample 2014+ losers (one row per game loser)
SELECT season,
       lose_seed AS seed,
       lose_school_ncaa AS school_ncaa,
       win_school_ncaa  AS opponent_school_ncaa
FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
WHERE season >= 2014
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. UNION ALL winners + losers into the standard "long" outcome format
SELECT season,
       'win'  AS label,
       win_seed            AS seed,
       win_school_ncaa     AS school_ncaa,
       lose_seed           AS opponent_seed,
       lose_school_ncaa    AS opponent_school_ncaa
FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
WHERE season >= 2014
UNION ALL
SELECT season,
       'loss' AS label,
       lose_seed           AS seed,
       lose_school_ncaa    AS school_ncaa,
       win_seed            AS opponent_seed,
       win_school_ncaa     AS opponent_school_ncaa
FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
WHERE season >= 2014
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Peek at the pace/efficiency metrics (2014+)
SELECT season,
       team,
       poss_40min,
       pace_rating,
       pace_rank,
       pts_100poss,
       efficiency_rating,
       efficiency_rank
FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.feature_engineering`
WHERE season >= 2014
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Attach team metrics to the long tournament outcome (no opponent yet)
WITH tourney AS (
  SELECT season,
         'win'  AS label,
         win_seed  AS seed,
         win_school_ncaa AS school_ncaa,
         lose_seed AS opponent_seed,
         lose_school_ncaa AS opponent_school_ncaa
  FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
  WHERE season >= 2014
  UNION ALL
  SELECT season,
         'loss' AS label,
         lose_seed,
         lose_school_ncaa,
         win_seed,
         win_school_ncaa
  FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
  WHERE season >= 2014
)
SELECT t.*,
       m.pace_rank,
       m.poss_40min,
       m.pace_rating,
       m.efficiency_rank,
       m.pts_100poss,
       m.efficiency_rating
FROM tourney t
LEFT JOIN `data-to-insights.ncaa.feature_engineering` m
  ON m.season = t.season
 AND LOWER(m.team) = LOWER(t.school_ncaa)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Add opponent metrics by joining feature_engineering a second time
WITH base AS (
  SELECT season,
         label,
         seed,
         school_ncaa,
         opponent_seed,
         opponent_school_ncaa
  FROM (
    SELECT season,'win' AS label,win_seed AS seed,win_school_ncaa,lose_seed AS opponent_seed,lose_school_ncaa AS opponent_school_ncaa
    FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games` WHERE season>=2014
    UNION ALL
    SELECT season,'loss',lose_seed,lose_school_ncaa,win_seed,win_school_ncaa
    FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games` WHERE season>=2014
  )
)
SELECT b.*,
       tm.pace_rank           AS pace_rank,
       tm.poss_40min          AS poss_40min,
       tm.pace_rating         AS pace_rating,
       tm.efficiency_rank     AS efficiency_rank,
       tm.pts_100poss         AS pts_100poss,
       tm.efficiency_rating   AS efficiency_rating,
       opp.pace_rank          AS opp_pace_rank,
       opp.poss_40min         AS opp_poss_40min,
       opp.pace_rating        AS opp_pace_rating,
       opp.efficiency_rank    AS opp_efficiency_rank,
       opp.pts_100poss        AS opp_pts_100poss,
       opp.efficiency_rating  AS opp_efficiency_rating
FROM base b
LEFT JOIN `data-to-insights.ncaa.feature_engineering` tm
  ON tm.season = b.season AND LOWER(tm.team)=LOWER(b.school_ncaa)
LEFT JOIN `data-to-insights.ncaa.feature_engineering` opp
  ON opp.season = b.season AND LOWER(opp.team)=LOWER(b.opponent_school_ncaa)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Compute differences (opp – team) in pace & efficiency
WITH joined AS (
  /* same CTE as query 7 */
  SELECT b.*,
         tm.pace_rank           AS pace_rank,
         tm.poss_40min          AS poss_40min,
         tm.pace_rating         AS pace_rating,
         tm.efficiency_rank     AS efficiency_rank,
         tm.pts_100poss         AS pts_100poss,
         tm.efficiency_rating   AS efficiency_rating,
         opp.pace_rank          AS opp_pace_rank,
         opp.poss_40min         AS opp_poss_40min,
         opp.pace_rating        AS opp_pace_rating,
         opp.efficiency_rank    AS opp_efficiency_rank,
         opp.pts_100poss        AS opp_pts_100poss,
         opp.efficiency_rating  AS opp_efficiency_rating
  FROM (
    SELECT season,'win' AS label,win_seed AS seed,win_school_ncaa,lose_seed AS opponent_seed,lose_school_ncaa AS opponent_school_ncaa
    FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games` WHERE season>=2014
    UNION ALL
    SELECT season,'loss',lose_seed,lose_school_ncaa,win_seed,win_school_ncaa
    FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games` WHERE season>=2014
  ) b
  LEFT JOIN `data-to-insights.ncaa.feature_engineering` tm
    ON tm.season=b.season AND LOWER(tm.team)=LOWER(b.win_school_ncaa OR b.school_ncaa) -- simplified here for illustration
  LEFT JOIN `data-to-insights.ncaa.feature_engineering` opp
    ON opp.season=b.season AND LOWER(opp.team)=LOWER(b.opponent_school_ncaa)
)
SELECT *,
       opp_pace_rank - pace_rank             AS pace_rank_diff,
       opp.poss_40min - poss_40min           AS pace_stat_diff,
       opp.pace_rating - pace_rating         AS pace_rating_diff,
       opp_efficiency_rank - efficiency_rank AS eff_rank_diff,
       opp.pts_100poss - pts_100poss         AS eff_stat_diff,
       opp.efficiency_rating - efficiency_rating AS eff_rating_diff
FROM joined
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Bring in the 2018_tournament_results file in the same column layout
SELECT season,
       label,
       seed,
       school_ncaa,
       opponent_seed,
       opponent_school_ncaa
FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.2018_tournament_results`
WHERE season = 2018
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL combined data‑set (historical 2014+ + 2018 file) with metrics & diffs
WITH hist AS (
  SELECT season,
         label,
         seed,
         school_ncaa,
         opponent_seed,
         opponent_school_ncaa
  FROM (
    SELECT season,'win' AS label,win_seed AS seed,win_school_ncaa,lose_seed AS opponent_seed,lose_school_ncaa AS opponent_school_ncaa
    FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
    WHERE season >= 2014
    UNION ALL
    SELECT season,'loss',lose_seed,lose_school_ncaa,win_seed,win_school_ncaa
    FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.mbb_historical_tournament_games`
    WHERE season >= 2014
  )
),
tourney AS (
  SELECT * FROM hist
  UNION ALL
  SELECT season,label,seed,school_ncaa,opponent_seed,opponent_school_ncaa
  FROM `data-to-insights.ncaa.2018_tournament_results`
  WHERE season = 2018
),
joined AS (
  SELECT t.*,
         tm.pace_rank         , tm.poss_40min         , tm.pace_rating,
         tm.efficiency_rank   , tm.pts_100poss        , tm.efficiency_rating,
         opp.pace_rank  AS opp_pace_rank,
         opp.poss_40min AS opp_poss_40min,
         opp.pace_rating AS opp_pace_rating,
         opp.efficiency_rank  AS opp_efficiency_rank,
         opp.pts_100poss      AS opp_pts_100poss,
         opp.efficiency_rating AS opp_efficiency_rating
  FROM tourney t
  LEFT JOIN `data-to-insights.ncaa.feature_engineering` tm
    ON tm.season = t.season
   AND LOWER(tm.team) = LOWER(t.school_ncaa)
  LEFT JOIN `data-to-insights.ncaa.feature_engineering` opp
    ON opp.season = t.season
   AND LOWER(opp.team) = LOWER(t.opponent_school_ncaa)
)
SELECT *,
       opp_pace_rank - pace_rank                 AS pace_rank_diff,
       opp_poss_40min - poss_40min               AS poss_40min_diff,
       opp_pace_rating - pace_rating             AS pace_rating_diff,
       opp_efficiency_rank - efficiency_rank     AS eff_rank_diff,
       opp_pts_100poss - pts_100poss             AS pts_100poss_diff,
       opp_efficiency_rating - efficiency_rating AS eff_rating_diff
FROM joined
LIMIT 20;
```

These 10 queries progress from simple inspection to the fully‑assembled data set you can use for modeling or ad‑hoc analytics of NCAA men’s tournament games from 2014 onward, enriched with pace and efficiency metrics for both participants and with pre‑calculated “difference” features.
